  "released": "2026-10-02",
  "min_app_version": "2026.1",
  "meta": {
    "title": "CMDS PID Catalog",
    "purpose": "Single source of truth for CMDS: maps a discovered switch PID to its family, IOS XE image train, and Meraki eligibility + minimum IOS XE for Configuration Source: Cloud and Configuration Source: Device.",
    "matching": "models[] entries are PID PREFIXES (case-insensitive). An exact PID match wins; otherwise the LONGEST matching prefix wins, so entry order never matters (e.g. C9300L-24P-4G beats C9300L-; C9350-48HXN beats C9350-48HX).",
    "statuses": {
      "supported": "Eligible; running IOS XE must be >= min_iosxe.",
      "not_eligible": "Meraki does not support this platform for this configuration source.",
      "future_release": "Meraki lists support as a future release; not onboardable yet.",
      "not_listed": "(implicit) group has no meraki block / PID not in catalog."
    },
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Cloud Management with IOS XE - supported models",
        "url": "https://documentation.meraki.com/Switching/Cloud_Management_with_IOS_XE",
        "reviewed": "2026-10-01",
        "page_updated": "2026-09-10"
      },
      {
        "title": "Enable Cloud Management for Cisco Switches with Device Configuration",
        "url": "https://documentation.meraki.com/Switching/Cloud_Management_with_IOS_XE/Install_and_Get_Started/Enable_Cloud_Management_for_Cisco_Switches_with_Device_Configuration",
        "reviewed": "2026-10-01",
        "page_updated": "2026-09-28"
      },
      {
        "title": "Cloud Configuration: Release Versions and Highlights",
        "url": "https://documentation.meraki.com/Switching/Cloud_Management_with_IOS_XE/Product_Information/Overviews_and_Datasheets/Cloud_Management_with_IOS_XE_Overview/Cloud_Configuration%3A_Release_Versions_and_Highlights",
        "reviewed": "2026-10-01",
        "page_updated": "2026-09-16"
      }
    ],
    "notes": [
      "Device Configuration minimum for C9200/C9200L/C9200CX and C9300/C9300L/C9300LM/C9300X is 17.15.3: the Device Configuration onboarding page says 17.15.3 while the main matrix says 17.15.1; CMDS uses the stricter 17.15.3 (Matt, 2026-10-01).",
      "C9350-24S/48S: main matrix says 26.1.2+ (Cloud and Device); the Device onboarding page mentions some C9350 models at 26.2.1. CMDS uses the matrix value - re-check when those models ship.",
      "Requirements for both sources: IOS XE in INSTALL mode (bundle mode unsupported) and a full-encryption image (NPE not supported).",
      "C9500 Device Configuration: onboarding does not modify device tracking; it can be changed via CLI afterwards (Meraki footnote).",
      "C9400/C9606 eligibility depends on the supervisor (Meraki lists C9400X-SUP-2/2XL and C9600-SUP-1/C9600X-SUP-2); the chassis PID alone cannot confirm the supervisor.",
      "Image trains carried over from CatOps (.27) platform_families.json; legacy (non-9k) families are image-train only and are never Meraki-eligible."
    ]
  },
